# Every fixture this grammar does not simply accept, and the list is exhaustive: a
# fixture missing from here must parse clean, and a name here that is no longer a
# fixture is a stale line. Seven fixtures are absent on purpose, because the fault in
# them is one no grammar of this language can see; docs/highlighting.md names all seven.

# Refused — the tree holds an ERROR or a MISSING node, which is what an editor paints
# red and what an incremental parser recovers from. The fault is in the shape.
invalid/bare-carriage-return.nuke refused
invalid/chained-dots.nuke refused
invalid/colon-instead-of-equals.nuke refused
invalid/comma-separator.nuke refused
invalid/comment-only.nuke refused
