# Named — the refinement `grammar/tokens.abnf` splits in two and `nuke-grammar` checks
# in a second pass over the tree. Longest match makes it one token here too, so a
# misspelling stays one bad number that names itself rather than two good ones: the
# document parses, and `malformed_number` is what an editor paints.
invalid/exponent-leading-zero.nuke named
invalid/exponent-plus.nuke named
invalid/list-double-zero.nuke named
invalid/list-leading-zero.nuke named
invalid/list-uppercase-exponent.nuke named
